Overlay patch 0018: extraction must not fsync per asset (D5's 9.2-min
first run). Mechanism, confirmed in code: Companion::Init unconditionally
sets the PROCESS-default spdlog level to debug + its own pattern
(Companion.cpp:133-134) — in-app that's LUS's file-sink logger with
flush_on(info) (LUS Context.cpp:174), and torch logs per-asset at info →
thousands of fsyncs into Documents/logs on a sandboxed FS.
Two hunks, one concern:
- torch/Companion.cpp: only stomp level/pattern when the caller asked for
  debug (gConfig.debug — the game passes false; the standalone CLI keeps
  its output at spdlog defaults). Upstreamable: a library must not
  reconfigure the host's global logger.
- GameExtractor.cpp GenerateOTR (__IOS__): quiet the default logger to
  `err` for the extraction window and restore after — errors and torch's
  final critical "Done!" still emit + flush; the per-asset chatter never
  reaches the sink. Desktop oracle unaffected.

--- a/torch/src/Companion.cpp
+++ b/torch/src/Companion.cpp
@@ -130,8 +130,13 @@
 
 void Companion::Init(const ExportType type) {
 
-    spdlog::set_level(spdlog::level::debug);
-    spdlog::set_pattern("[%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S.%e] [%l] %v");
+    // Only reconfigure the process-wide logger when debug output was
+    // requested: as an embedded library (SpaghettiKart in-app extraction)
+    // the host owns the default logger, and its sink may flush per line.
+    if (this->gConfig.debug) {
+        spdlog::set_level(spdlog::level::debug);
+        spdlog::set_pattern("[%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S.%e] [%l] %v");
+    }
 
     this->gConfig.exporterType = type;
     this->RegisterFactory("BLOB", std::make_shared<BlobFactory>());
--- a/src/port/GameExtractor.cpp
+++ b/src/port/GameExtractor.cpp
@@ -192,11 +192,25 @@
     Companion::Instance = new Companion(this->mGameData, ArchiveType::O2R, false, assets_path, game_path);
     Companion::Instance->SetAdditionalFiles({ "meta/mods.toml" });
 
+#ifdef __IOS__
+    // LUS's default logger flushes on every info line into Documents/logs;
+    // torch logs per asset. That made first-run extraction take 9.2 min on
+    // the simulator (overlay 0018 / D5). Quiet to err for the extraction
+    // window; errors and the final critical summary still emit.
+    const auto sohIosPrevLevel = spdlog::get_level();
+    spdlog::set_level(spdlog::level::err);
+#endif
+
+    bool sohExtractOk = true;
     try {
         Companion::Instance->Init(ExportType::Binary);
     } catch (const std::exception& e) {
-        return false;
+        sohExtractOk = false;
     }
 
-    return true;
+#ifdef __IOS__
+    spdlog::set_level(sohIosPrevLevel);
+#endif
+
+    return sohExtractOk;
 }
